+ * Listens to game controllers on /dev/input and turns them into keyboard
+ * navigation events for the on-screen keyboard.
+ *
+ * Devices are discovered by their evdev capabilities, so anything the kernel
+ * reports as a gamepad works (Xbox, DualSense, Switch Pro, 8BitDo, ...).
+ * Hotplugging is handled by watching /dev/input for new device nodes.
+ *
+ * Directions come from the d-pad (either as a hat axis or as buttons) and from
+ * the left analog stick, and auto-repeat while held. Everything else is
+ * reported as a high level Action so the caller can decide what to do with it.
+ *
